  "summary_en": "UK Act establishing insurer liability for accidents caused by self-driving automated vehicles in Great Britain, with a Secretary of State list of automated vehicles, rules on software alterations and updates, and regulation-making powers for electric vehicle charging infrastructure. Includes limitation-period amendments; later partly amended by the Automated Vehicles Act 2024.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Secretary of State must list vehicles capable of safely driving themselves.",
   "Insurer (or owner if uninsured) is liable for damage from accidents caused by automated vehicles driving themselves.",
   "Insurers may limit liability for unauthorised software alterations or failure to install safety-critical updates.",
   "Insurer can recover from other liable parties; contributory negligence applies.",
   "Part 2 gives powers to regulate public charge point access, standards, smart charging and data."
  ],
